{"path":"io/manip/ends","title":"std::ends","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::</span>ends","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/io/manip/ends","section":"io","kind":"page","summary":"Inserts a null character into the output sequence os as if by calling os.put(CharT()).","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/ostream\">&lt;ostream&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl\">\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\"> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> CharT, <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> Traits <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_ostream\"><span class=\"kw1732\">std::<span class=\"me2\">basic_ostream</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>CharT, Traits<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> ends<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_ostream\"><span class=\"kw1732\">std::<span class=\"me2\">basic_ostream</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>CharT, Traits<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> os <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Inserts a null character into the output sequence <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">os</span></code> as if by calling <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">os.<span class=\"me1\">put</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>CharT<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>. \n</p><p>This is an output-only I/O manipulator, it may be called with an expression such as <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">out <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">ends</span></span></code> for any <code>out</code> of type <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_ostream\">std::basic_ostream</a></span>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>This manipulator is typically used with <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/ostrstream\"><span class=\"kw1771\">std::<span class=\"me2\">ostrstream</span></span></a></span></code>, when the associated output buffer needs to be null-terminated to be processed as a C string.\n</p><p>Unlike <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/manip/endl\">std::endl</a></span>, this manipulator does not flush the stream.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> os\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> reference to output stream\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">os</span></code> (reference to the stream after insertion of the null character).\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;cstdio&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;strstream&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/ostrstream\"><span class=\"kw1771\">std::<span class=\"me2\">ostrstream</span></span></a> oss<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    oss <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"Sample text: \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"nu0\">42</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">ends</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/c/fprintf\"><span class=\"kw1861\">std::<span class=\"me2\">printf</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"%s<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span>, oss.<span class=\"me1\">str</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    oss.<span class=\"me1\">freeze</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw2\">false</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"co1\">// enable memory deallocation</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>Sample text: 42</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/ostrstream\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>ostrstream</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-deprecated-cxx98\">(deprecated in C++98)</span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-until-cxx26\">(removed in C++26)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  implements character array output operations <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(class)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"io","title":"Input/output library"},{"path":"io/manip","title":"Input/output manipulators"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::ends","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration. Inserts a null character into the output sequence os as if by calling os.put(CharT())."},{"label":"Notes","note":"This manipulator is typically used with std::ostrstream, when the associated output buffer needs to be null-terminated to be processed as a C string."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"os"},{"label":"Return value","note":"os (reference to the stream after insertion of the null character)."},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"ostrstream","note":"implements character array output operations"}]}]},"standards":["C++98","C++26"],"wordCount":151,"codeBlockCount":2}
